<section class="ev-hero"><div class="ev-w ev-hero-g"><div><p class="ev-chip">For self-taught language learners</p><h1>Learn a language <span>the steady way.</span></h1><p class="ev-lead">Eduvana is an independent education site for adults learning a new language on their own. Set realistic goals, build vocabulary that sticks and practise a little every day.</p><p class="ev-acts"><a class="btn" href="#tools">Plan my learning</a><a class="ev-ln" href="language-learning-guide.html">Read the learning plan</a></p></div><div class="ev-hero-f"><img src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1794675077621-f2ed3d3f29d7?auto=format&fit=crop&w=560&h=620&q=75" alt="woman reading a book at a window seat in a cafe" width="560" height="620" fetchpriority="high"><div class="ev-bub ev-b1">&iexcl;Hola!</div><div class="ev-bub ev-b2">Bonjour</div><div class="ev-bub ev-b3">Ciao</div></div></div></section>

<section class="ev-s"><div class="ev-w"><div class="ev-t"><h2>Four skills, one balanced week</h2><p>Every language has four skills. Neglect one and the others slow down.</p></div><div class="ev-four"><div><b>Listen</b><p>Podcasts, short videos and audio with transcripts, every day.</p><span>30%</span></div><div><b>Speak</b><p>Shadowing, reading aloud and short conversations.</p><span>25%</span></div><div><b>Read</b><p>Graded readers, news for learners, subtitles in the target language.</p><span>25%</span></div><div><b>Write</b><p>A short daily journal or messages to a language partner.</p><span>20%</span></div></div></div></section>

<section id="tools" class="ev-tools">
<div class="ev-band ev-band1"><div class="ev-w ev-bg"><div class="ev-bt"><p class="ev-chip">Tool 1</p><h2>Vocabulary Goal Planner</h2><p>How long until you reach your word target?</p><img src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1794338288772-69ccad0042d4?auto=format&fit=crop&w=520&h=300&q=75" alt="person holding an open book with page markers" width="520" height="300" loading="lazy"></div><div class="ev-card"><label for="vg-n">Words you know now<input id="vg-n" type="number" min="0" max="20000" step="50" value="300"></label><label for="vg-t">Target<select id="vg-t"><option value="1000">1,000 words (everyday basics)</option><option value="2000" selected>2,000 words (most daily speech)</option><option value="3000">3,000 words (comfortable reading)</option><option value="5000">5,000 words (advanced)</option></select></label><label for="vg-d">New words per day<input id="vg-d" type="number" min="1" max="100" value="10"></label><div class="ev-out" id="vg-o" aria-live="polite"></div></div></div></div>
<div class="ev-band ev-band2"><div class="ev-w ev-bg ev-bg-r"><div class="ev-bt"><p class="ev-chip">Tool 2</p><h2>Practice Streak Planner</h2><p>See what small daily sessions add up to.</p><img src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1794897159348-73c02c76930f?auto=format&fit=crop&w=520&h=300&q=75" alt="person sitting at a desk with a lamp" width="520" height="300" loading="lazy"></div><div class="ev-card"><label for="ps-m">Minutes per session<input id="ps-m" type="number" min="5" max="180" step="5" value="20"></label><label for="ps-d">Days per week<input id="ps-d" type="number" min="1" max="7" value="5"></label><div class="ev-out" id="ps-o" aria-live="polite"></div></div></div></div>
<div class="ev-band ev-band3"><div class="ev-w ev-bg"><div class="ev-bt"><p class="ev-chip">Tool 3</p><h2>Language Level Estimator</h2><p>A rough guide to the hours a level takes.</p><img src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1794241110561-485c9d98d04c?auto=format&fit=crop&w=520&h=300&q=75" alt="open book resting on a wooden surface" width="520" height="300" loading="lazy"></div><div class="ev-card"><label for="ll-l">Language (for English speakers)<select id="ll-l"><option value="1">Spanish, French, Italian, Portuguese</option><option value="1.5">German, Indonesian, Swahili</option><option value="2">Russian, Greek, Hindi, Turkish</option><option value="3">Japanese, Mandarin, Arabic, Korean</option></select></label><label for="ll-g">Goal level<select id="ll-g"><option value="a2">A2: basic everyday use</option><option value="b1" selected>B1: independent in familiar situations</option><option value="b2">B2: comfortable conversation</option><option value="c1">C1: advanced</option></select></label><label for="ll-h">Hours per week you can study<input id="ll-h" type="number" min="1" max="40" value="5"></label><div class="ev-out" id="ll-o" aria-live="polite"></div></div></div></div>
</section>

<section class="ev-s"><div class="ev-w ev-lib"><figure><img src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1794340733964-a57394b8af7f?auto=format&fit=crop&w=560&h=640&q=75" alt="rows of books on wooden library shelves" width="560" height="640" loading="lazy"></figure><div><h2>A simple daily routine</h2><ol class="ev-rt"><li><time>5 min</time><span>Review yesterday&rsquo;s words with flashcards.</span></li><li><time>10 min</time><span>Listen to something short, then again with a transcript.</span></li><li><time>5 min</time><span>Learn ten new words in a sentence, not alone.</span></li><li><time>5 min</time><span>Say three sentences out loud about your day.</span></li></ol><p>Twenty-five minutes, every day, beats three hours on a Sunday.</p></div></div></section>

<section class="ev-s ev-mint"><div class="ev-w"><div class="ev-t"><h2>Read the guides</h2></div><div class="ev-gds"><a href="language-learning-guide.html"><img src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1794672205307-fc13eca81cd1?auto=format&fit=crop&w=640&h=400&q=75" alt="multi-level library interior" width="640" height="400" loading="lazy"><div><small>Guide 1</small><h3>The Language Learning Guide</h3><p>Goals, CEFR levels, a weekly plan and how to keep going when progress feels slow.</p></div></a><a href="vocabulary-guide.html"><img src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1794192197522-b04e41323a33?auto=format&fit=crop&w=640&h=400&q=75" alt="small community book exchange box" width="640" height="400" loading="lazy"><div><small>Guide 2</small><h3>The Vocabulary Guide</h3><p>Which words to learn first, how to remember them and how to move them into speech.</p></div></a></div></div></section>

<section class="ev-s"><div class="ev-w ev-fq"><div class="ev-t ev-t-l"><h2>Learner questions</h2><p>Short, honest answers.</p></div><div class="ev-faq"><details open><summary>How long does it take to learn a language?</summary><p>It depends on the language, your native language and how you practise. As a rough guide, English speakers often need several hundred hours to hold everyday conversations in a closely related language such as Spanish, and considerably more for languages like Japanese or Arabic.</p></details><details><summary>How many words do I need to know?</summary><p>Around 1,000 common words cover a large share of everyday conversation, and 2,000&ndash;3,000 let you follow most daily speech and simple texts. Learn the most frequent words first.</p></details><details><summary>Is it better to study every day or for longer once a week?</summary><p>Short daily practice usually beats one long weekly session. Regular contact with the language keeps words fresh and builds the habit.</p></details><details><summary>What are the CEFR levels?</summary><p>A common European scale from A1 (beginner) to C2 (mastery). A2 is basic everyday use, B1 is independent in familiar situations, B2 is comfortable conversation and C1 is advanced.</p></details><details><summary>Should I learn grammar first?</summary><p>Learn enough grammar to build simple sentences, then keep adding it alongside vocabulary and listening. Grammar makes more sense once you have heard it used.</p></details><details><summary>How can I practise speaking alone?</summary><p>Read aloud, shadow audio by repeating it just after the speaker, describe what you are doing out loud and record yourself. Then look for a conversation partner when you can.</p></details></div></div></section>

<section class="ev-nl"><div class="ev-w ev-nl-g"><div><h2>The Eduvana Note</h2><p>A monthly email with one learning technique and one motivating idea.</p></div><a class="btn" href="mailto:hello@eduvana.com?subject=The%20Eduvana%20Note&amp;body=Please%20subscribe%20me.">Subscribe by email</a></div></section>

